# pen_release_witness.rish -- a runner that makes a throwaway pen and never removes it.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/pen_release_witness.rish
#
# THE THIRD QUESTION ABOUT ONE PEN. `shared_pen` reads whether a pen is CONTENDED -- one constant
# name, eight checkouts. `pen_entry` reads whether a pen is ENTERED -- REDS %729, a case body that
# ran at the repository root. Neither reads whether it is RELEASED, and REDS %745 is what that
# costs: `tools/am/amphora_mark_wreck_witness.rish` makes a 24MB pen with `mktemp -d` and never
# removes it, so nine days of a rostered witness put 1,312 pens and 32G into the shared /tmp, the
# pier read 990M free, and the first instrument to notice was a `pwd` builtin answering
# `write error: No space left on device`.
#
# AND THE TWO STANDING GUARDS READ ONE LANGUAGE. `pen_entry`'s population is `git ls-files '*.sh'`
# plus a POSIX shell shebang, and a Rishi source in this tree carries neither -- so the runner that
# actually filled the pier stood outside the pen family's whole population. This reading opens
# both, 461 shell runners and 338 Rishi sources carrying a pen between them.
#
# A RATCHET RATHER THAN A WALL, deliberately. Sixteen runners made a pen and removed it nowhere at
# seating, fourteen of them Rishi witnesses in the amphora and caravan families; each repair belongs
# to its owning lane, and a wall seated here would red every ship for faults no lap of theirs may
# touch. The ceiling only falls, and it stands at eight.
#
# `unreleased_on_refusal` -- the runners whose removal stands on the straight-line success path, so
# a refusal above it leaves the pen behind -- is REPORTED and gated by nothing. In shell the cure
# is a `trap` reaching the removal. It read 341 at seating, 324 from `20260916.061500`, and 312
# from `20260916.073000`; run the scan rather than trusting any of the three.
#
# THAT LAST FALL MOVED NO FILE. This header said the cure is *the `trap 'rm -rf "$pen"' EXIT`
# every control in tools/fixtures/ already carries*, and the scan required exactly that one-line
# spelling, so the two-line form -- a `cleanup()` function above a `trap cleanup EXIT` -- read as
# a leak. Measured: of 323 controls under `tools/fixtures/`, 287 spell the trap inline and 9 spell
# it as a function, so the sentence was true of the majority and the predicate was built on it.
# Those nine were the miscounted ones. In the class itself, 12 of the 18 shell files were this
# shape -- `tools/fixtures/a/aurora_placement_control.sh` releases on EXIT, INT, TERM and HUP and
# was counted a leak. The GATED `never_removed` reading never moved, because the function body
# sets `removed` either way: the fault was confined to the reported half, which is the half a ship
# reads as its work queue. A count of 324 sent a lane converting files already correct.
#
# THE RISHI HALF OF THAT SENTENCE IS CLOSED, and the elder claim beside it was false. This header
# read *Rishi has no trap*; the runtime has carried a CleanupRegistry since `acquire-lock`, and
# what it lacked was a pen kind. `make-pen` seats one (`tools/r/rishi_make_pen_witness.rish`): the
# runtime composes the path, creates the directory, and releases it recursively after a return, a
# refusal, an `exit`, HUP, INT, or TERM. A Rishi source in the second class is now a source
# awaiting one line rather than one awaiting a language.
#
# `runtime_pens` counts the sources that have taken it, and it enters NEITHER class -- the two
# populations are disjoint by construction, so a conversion moves a file between readings rather
# than out of the census. A count that fell because a file left the population would read exactly
# like a repair.
#
# AND THE FIRST WHOLE-ROOM CONVERSION PROVED THAT CLAUSE EARNS ITS PLACE. On `20260916.061500` the
# nineteen `tools/am/` witnesses took `make-pen` together: `runtime_pens` 2 to 21,
# `unreleased_on_refusal` 342 to 324, and `never_removed` 9 to 8. THE ONE THAT LEFT THE GATED
# READING WAS NEVER A LEAK -- it is `amphora_restore_negative_witness.rish`, the false positive
# %758 booked, which swept its pen in Rishi's argv spelling `run ["rm" "-rf" home]` where this
# predicate requires a `$` sigil. Read the ceiling's own arc in the scan before reading that fall
# as a repair. The conversion was proven from both sides rather than asserted: one planted refusal,
# placed identically, leaves one pen behind under the elder shape and none under this one.
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pen_release_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "pen release scan did not run: ${scan.err_brief}"
assert scan.out contains "never_removed=8" else "the never-removed population moved: ${scan.out_brief}"
assert scan.out contains "ceiling_ok=yes" else "pen release over its ceiling: ${scan.out_brief}"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=released" else "pen release verdict missing: ${scan.out_brief}"

# THE CONTROL IS ASSERTED BESIDE THE READING, because a ratchet proven only in the passing
# direction cannot be told from a reading that counts nothing. Forty-six behaviors on real git
# repositories in a throwaway pen, every refusal planted and then lifted, the ceiling shown from
# both sides, and three mutations -- the continuation join, the transitive pen variable, and the
# trap reading -- each required to bite and then required to walk free unmutated.
#
# THE LEG TALLY IS ASSERTED BESIDE THE VERDICT, so a leg written tomorrow is heard the day it
# lands: `control_verdict=ok` says only that the control reached its last line.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/pen_release_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "pen release control did not reach control_verdict=ok: ${control.out_brief}"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "pen release control verdict missing: ${control.out_brief}"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "a planted behavior went unread: ${control.out_brief}"
assert control.out contains "pass=55" else "the control's leg tally moved: ${control.out_brief}"

assert scan.out contains "runtime_pens=21" else "the runtime-owned pen population moved: ${scan.out_brief}"

say "GREEN: every pen this tree makes is counted for its release -- 8 never removed under a ceiling that only falls, and 21 handed to the runtime."
